SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a stripe that the face at its end cuts to a point on an edge at
the spine's end vertex runs a seam of that face, which ends at the vertex
along the edge's line, on to the point, as the corner does for an OnSame
end whose opposite contact ends on the prolonged edge (patch 1331)
(mitcad#1422).

A plate's top edge rounded as a tangent chain up to a boss whose cylinder
the plate's flat sides go on into tangentially: the contact on the top
meets the boss's foot short of the vertex, and the contact on the side
touches the cylinder on the vertical edge below the vertex. Where the
analytic blend's pieces were split with the contact on the top ending at
the foot (the stripe's faces in the other order, the chain picked at its
other side), ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd cuts the blend with the cylinder down to
the vertical edge, the stripe ending in a point there (FreeBoundary), and
the corner is not made. The cylinder then grows down across its seam's
line from the vertex to that point, but the seam stopped at the vertex:
the cylinder's face lost the boss above the plate (an unorientable face).

PerformFilletOnVertex now runs the seam on for a lone stripe ending so
(ChFi3d_SeamRunOnAtPointEnd, both end points on one edge at the vertex),
with patch 1331's ChFi3d_SeamRunOnAlongEdge, made visible to it.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_boss_tangent.cpp, the plate's top edge
picked at its other side (y = -25) rounded with 1, 3 and 6, alone and with
the boss's top edge, on the synthetic bodies and on the body MitCad's UI
builds from a slot and a circle (MITCAD_GEOMETRY_CASES): valid, the
material removed as the exact one within 1e-6 of it.

Upstream: new.

